2026-06-22 14:17:12,186 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 14:17:12,186 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: We can propose an AI-powered assistant that leverages our retrieval-augmented generation capabilities, grounded in the hospital's own validated documents, to support clinical-administrative activities. The core approach will utilize hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, and multi-document synthesis to provide relevant information and drafting assistance.

The assistant can be designed to provide template-guided drafting for medical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries and medical correspondence, as well as structured extraction to assist with tasks like PMSI/ICD-10 coding. Additionally, the system can recall applicable rules and regulations during dossier handling and suggest next steps based on the dossier context.

To ensure continuity of care, the assistant can generate structured handover summaries, allowing professionals to efficiently take over in-progress dossiers with full context. Our iterative approach will involve corpus selection and curation with the hospital's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop to measure answer quality.

In terms of innovation strategy, we can embed the assistant into the hospital staff's existing work environment and tools, avoiding disruption to clinical or administrative workflows. The assistant will be designed to augment existing practices, with staff interacting through their current interfaces. This approach has demonstrated efficiency outcomes in comparable deployments, reducing processing and documentation times by surfacing information and drafting content at the point of need.

Our prior experience with a medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group can serve as a relevant reference point for this project, providing valuable insights into the development and deployment of such an assistant.
